the latest ps5 showcase revealed the  next gen console's release date and  price  plus some new game announcements let's  talk about everything you need to know  first and foremost the ps5 will be  launching on november 12th  in the us canada mexico japan  australia new zealand and south korea  europe and the rest of the world can get  their hands on it on november 19th  the standard ps5 will cost you 500 us  dollars  while the all digital edition which has  no disk drive will be 400 bucks  check gamespot for more pricing info for  your region so what games can you  actually play on launch day  you can jump into assassin's creed  valhalla demon souls devil may cry 5  special edition  and spider-man miles morales there are  also a ton of games coming to ps5  at or around launch day and that list is  a lot longer  that list includes deep breath black ops  cold war  bug snacks godfall immortals phoenix  rising marvel's avengers ratchet and  clank rift apart  and a bunch more you can see the  complete list on gamespot  and take note a lot of these games are  gonna be sold for 70 bucks a pop  instead of the 60 we're used to paying  for games right now  you'll also be able to play backwards  compatible ps4 games  sony previously said that the 100 most  popular ps4 games will be playable on  day one  with more to come what's more the  showcase revealed the playstation plus  collection  ps plus subscribers can download and  play a bunch of ps4 favorites on ps5 on  day one  including god of war persona 5 until  dawn  days gone and more that seems like a  great way to play any physical ps4 games  you already own if you decide to go with  the diskless ps5 model  now if you're concerned about having  enough storage to keep and play all  these games  good news the ps5 comes with an 825 gig  solid-state drive what's more you can  increase your storage with third-party  drives if you wish  that said sony hasn't given its  recommendations for what ssds will work  best with the ps5 architecture  so you should wait before committing to  one keep an eye on gamespot for any news  on that front  and stay tuned as we keep covering the  ps5 with handy videos like this  and our weekly show generation next i  know i'm excited to hear more about  final fantasy 16  and that god of war sequel  you
 

